# engine-strict is deliberately NOT set here; `pnpm node:check` replaces it.
#
# It was set, for a good reason: React Router 8 needs Node >= 22.22, `engines` is
# documentation unless something enforces it, and this repository has no CI. But
# engine-strict honours every publisher's `engines`, and one of them is not a
# requirement: `cedict-json` pins `node: "22"` on a package that is 16 MB of JSON
# and an 89-byte re-export we never execute. That pin rejected Node 24 while
# react-router rejected Vercel's 22.x image, so no Node available to a Vercel
# build satisfied both, and every deploy died in `pnpm install`.
#
# The floor is now checked by `scripts/check-node.ts`, which runs first in
# `pnpm build` and states the real requirement. See docs/deploy.md §1.
